ood use</span>\n  <span>build ... out of</span>\n  <span>pull down</span>\n  <span>set up</span>\n  <span>known for</span>\n  <span>not only ... but also</span>\n</div>\n\n<div class=\"exercise-box\">\n  <ol>\n    <li>Amy Hayes lives in the UK. Many of the old buildings in her neighborhood were <span class=\"blank\">pulled down</span>.</li>\n    <li>All the rubbish and old things in Amy's neighborhood were then <span class=\"blank blank-long\">put to good use</span> when Amy built her house.</li>\n    <li>Amy is very creative. She <span class=\"blank\">built</span> her front gate <span class=\"blank\">out of</span> rocks and old glass bottles. She put an old boat on top of her house.</li>\n    <li>Jessica Wong sells her bags in a small shop, but she has also <span class=\"blank\">set up</span> an online business to sell them.</li>\n    <li>Though Jessica's bags are made from old clothes, her bags are <span class=\"blank blank-long\">known for</span> being cute and useful.</li>\n    <li>Wang Tao <span class=\"blank\">not only</span> makes large pieces of metal art that look like animals or humans, <span class=\"blank\">but also</span> makes smaller pieces for the home.</li>\n  </ol>\n</div>\n\n<div>\n  <span class=\"section-label\">2d</span>\n  <span class=\"section-title\">Underline the words in the passage based on the words below. What are the differences?</span>\n</div>\n\n<div class=\"word-bank\">\n  <div class=\"word-pair\"><span class=\"top\">rethink</span><span class=\"bottom\">think</span></div>\n  <div class=\"word-pair\"><span class=\"top\">useful/</span><span class=\"bottom\">use</span></div>\n  <div class=\"word-pair\"><span class=\"top\">reuse</span><span class=\"bottom\">use</span></div>\n  <div class=\"word-pair\"><span class=\"top\">unusual</span><span class=\"bottom\">usual</span></div>\n  <div class=\"word-pair\"><span class=\"top\">recycling</span><span class=\"bottom\">recycle</span></div>\n  <div class=\"word-pair\"><span class=\"top\">building<